{
  "name": "How to Prepare for a Storm Damage Roof Inspection in Addison",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1: Document the Damage Safely",
      "text": "When a storm hits Addison, your first priority is safety. Once it's safe, take photos or videos of any visible damage from the ground, both exterior (roof, gutters, siding) and interior (any leaks or water stains). Note the date and time you first noticed the damage. This documentation helps establish the timeline and extent of the storm's impact, which is really useful for insurance or a professional assessment.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 2: Collect Relevant Information",
      "text": "Gather any documents related to your roof, like its age, material, and any past repair records. If you have your insurance policy handy, know your policy number and provider details. This information gives your inspector a better understanding of your roof's history and helps them assess damage in context. It also speeds up any potential insurance claims process.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 3: Clear the Inspection Area",
      "text": "Make sure there's clear access around your home for the inspection team. Move any outdoor furniture, vehicles, or potted plants that might be in the way. If you have pets, make arrangements for them to be safely indoors during the inspection. A clear path ensures the inspection can be conducted efficiently and safely, minimizing any potential hazards for the inspectors.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 4: Communicate Your Concerns",
      "text": "Before the inspection begins, talk to your inspector about any specific concerns you have or areas where you suspect damage. Point out anything unusual you've observed, like fallen debris, granule loss, or specific areas of the roof that look different. Your insights can guide the inspector to focus on critical areas and ensure a comprehensive evaluation.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 4
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 5: Ask About the Process",
      "text": "Don't hesitate to ask your inspector about their methods, what they'll be looking for, and how they'll document their findings. Understand if they'll be walking the roof or using drone technology, and what kind of report you can expect afterward. Being informed helps you understand the thoroughness of the inspection and what to expect from the results.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 5
    }
  ],
  "@type": "HowTo",
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "speakable": {
    "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
    "cssSelector": [
      "h1",
      ".howto-step",
      "[itemprop=\"step\"]"
    ]
  },
